sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client
  participant RID as RequestId
  participant AUTH as Auth
  participant RL as RateLimit
  participant AUD as Audit
  participant CO as Coordinator
  participant PG as Postgres via pgBouncer
  participant MS as model-server sidecar
  participant RD as Redis

  C->>RID: GET /users/{id}/recommendations
  RID->>RID: adopt X-Request-ID if 1-128 printable ASCII,<br/>otherwise mint a UUID

  RID->>AUTH: dispatch
  AUTH->>AUTH: RS256 verify against the TTL-cached JWKS
  AUTH->>AUTH: tenant = realm from the issuer path,<br/>never a client-declared claim
  AUTH->>AUTH: require aud=movielens-api and an allow-listed azp
  AUTH->>PG: BEGIN, SET LOCAL app.tenant_id
  AUTH->>PG: SELECT 1 FROM public.tenants
  Note over AUTH,PG: A verified realm with no tenant row is a 403,<br/>not a 401 — the token is fine, the tenant is not

  AUTH->>RL: dispatch
  RL->>RL: token bucket per (tenant, subject) — 600/min, burst 120, per worker
  Note over RL,AUD: Every response carries X-RateLimit-*.<br/>A refusal is 429 + Retry-After and writes no audit row.

  RL->>AUD: dispatch
  AUD->>CO: recommend
  CO->>PG: one UNION ALL read of user_movie_state:<br/>positives (watched, not dismissed)<br/>+ exclusions (dismissals + already seen)

  alt positives < 5
    CO->>PG: popularity, exclusions applied in SQL
    Note over CO,PG: serving_policy.name = popularity, learned = false, reason = cold-start
  else positives >= 5
    CO->>MS: POST /rank, bearer, 0.5 s timeout
    MS->>MS: CandidateIndex.retrieve — only dismissals may drop a seed
    MS->>RD: batched Feast read of 8 features per candidate
    RD-->>MS: feature matrix + oldest event time
    MS->>MS: LightGBM scores and orders
    MS-->>CO: ranked items, seed_count, candidate sources
    CO->>PG: hydrate metadata, exclusions re-applied
    CO->>CO: final fail-closed exclusion sweep
    Note over CO,MS: seed_count > 0 → item-item-cosine+lightgbm, learned = true<br/>seed_count = 0 → popularity-fill+lightgbm, learned = false
  end

  CO->>PG: INSERT recommendation_audits on the same RLS connection
  AUTH->>PG: COMMIT
  Note over AUTH,PG: The commit precedes the response.<br/>No 2xx for an audit row that could still fail to land.
  AUTH-->>C: 200 with serving_policy, X-Request-ID, X-RateLimit-*

  Note over C,RD: CI gate 2026-08-20 — p50 6.31 ms, p95 14.27 ms, p99 41.30 ms<br/>Production-topology rehearsal 2026-08-27 — p50 6.85 ms, p95 9.47 ms, p99 12.93 ms<br/>SLO — p99 < 100 ms, zero errors, more than 50 requests/second
